     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    Sorry to bother - I loaded plyr as suggested<br>\r\n qplot(cut,depth,data=diamonds,geom=&quot;boxplot&quot;,group=round_any(carat,0.1,floor),<br>\r\n    + xlim=c(0,3))<br>\r\n    error: Discrete value supplied to continuous scale<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    Hope I didn&#39;t make further errors - <br>\r\n    best wishes<br>\r\n    Troels<br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <div>Den 28-01-2015 kl. 15:53 skrev\r\n      <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      <div style=\"border:1px solid #d3d3d3;max-width:850px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000\">\r\n        <div style=\"background-color:#f5f5f5;padding:10px 20px\">\r\n          <table style=\"width:100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n            <tbody>\r\n              <tr>\r\n                <td style=\"width:70%\"> <span style=\"font:18px/20px arial;color:#333333\"> <a style=\"text-decoration:none;color:#333333\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n                      ggp...@googlegroups.com</a> </span> </td>\r\n                <td style=\"text-align:right;width:30%\"> <span style=\"font:20px/24px arial\"><a style=\"color:#dd4b39;text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#%21overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23%2521overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369699250000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ejpfnGu0XkS85eqLg692b\">Google Groups</a></span> </td>\r\n                <td style=\"width:32px\"> <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#%21overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23%2521overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369699250000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ejpfnGu0XkS85eqLg692b\"><img style=\"border:0;vertical-align:middle\" src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/4SGWHe9midrWMDxDIJMQraTMMgnAU71soPZ0D28IOSZcs66TdyRoCqyIhaTt-kwo0YKv2lRo05RkwsGFZdnFhdvy60XdxNlL2U-B=s0-d-e1-ft#http://www.google.com/images/icons/product/groups-32.png\"></a>\r\n                </td>\r\n              </tr>\r\n            </tbody>\r\n          </table>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div style=\"padding:20px;background-color:#f5f5f5\">\r\n          <div style=\"font-family:arial;color:#222222;padding:0px\">\r\n            <a name=\"m_2970457510136618189_digest_top\" style=\"font-size:21px\" rel=\"nofollow\"> Topic digest </a><br>\r\n            <span style=\"font-size:11px\"> <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"nofollow\">View\r\n                all topics</a> </span>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <div style=\"font:13px/18px arial;color:#222222;padding:0px;margin-bottom:30px\">\r\n            <ul style=\"margin-left:3px;padding-left:0px\">\r\n              <li> <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_2970457510136618189_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\"> round_any()</a> - <span style=\"color:#777777\">2 Updates</span> </li>\r\n              <li> <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_2970457510136618189_group_thread_1\" rel=\"nofollow\"> barplot - fixed width of bars</a>\r\n                - <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span> </li>\r\n              <li> <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_2970457510136618189_group_thread_2\" rel=\"nofollow\"> Rcpp dependency not installed\r\n                  - was &quot;RE: [R] installing Packages&quot;</a> - <span style=\"color:#777777\">1 Update</span> </li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <a name=\"m_2970457510136618189_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a>\r\n          <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\"> <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/t/b7a3248d91a9c79d?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/t/b7a3248d91a9c79d?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369699250000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2INQ8PsvIa4cspRjTc_K2B\"> round_any() </a> </div>\r\n          <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n            <tbody>\r\n              <tr>\r\n                <td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\"> <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\"> Troels Ring\r\n                    <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;tr...@gvdnet.dk&gt;</a>: Jan 28 05:57AM -0800 </span>\r\n                  <br>\r\n                  <br>\r\n                  Hi, sorry to ask simple questions, but in the ggplot2\r\n                  book on p 71 an <br>\r\n                  example uses a founction round_any() - which not seems\r\n                  to be known. Any <br>\r\n                  solutions?<br>\r\n                  All best wishes<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  Troels<br>\r\n                </td>\r\n              </tr>\r\n              <tr>\r\n                <td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\"> <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\"> &quot;Roman Luštrik&quot;\r\n                    <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;roman....@gmail.com&gt;</a>: Jan 28 03:16PM\r\n                    +0100 </span> <br>\r\n                  <br>\r\n                  I googled &quot;round_any() ggplot&quot; and the first page that\r\n                  popped up was<br>\r\n                  <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_boxplot.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_boxplot.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369699250000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1WRyWYcsCm_ONywnsh0Adi\">http://docs.ggplot2.org/0.9.3.1/geom_boxplot.html</a><br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  If I ctrl+f to &quot;round_any()&quot; it says:<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  # Scales vs. coordinate transforms ------- # Scale\r\n                  transformations occur<br>\r\n                  before the boxplot statistics are computed. #\r\n                  Coordinate transformations<br>\r\n                  occur afterwards. Observe the effect on the # number\r\n                  of outliers.<br>\r\n                  library(plyr) # to access round_any m &lt;-\r\n                  ggplot(movies, aes(y = votes, x =<br>\r\n                  rating, group = round_any(rating, 0.5))) m +\r\n                  geom_boxplot()<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  In short, you need to load the plyr package to be able\r\n                  to use this function.<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  Cheers,<br>\r\n                  Roman<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  -- <br>\r\n                  In God we trust, all others bring data.<br>\r\n                </td>\r\n              </tr>\r\n            </tbody>\r\n          </table>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\"> <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_2970457510136618189_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\">Back to top</a> </div>\r\n          <a name=\"m_2970457510136618189_group_thread_1\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a>\r\n          <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\"> <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/t/52a711f8fa9d518e?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/t/52a711f8fa9d518e?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369699250000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2l6PNecc8pYNDSR5uLcaIq\"> barplot - fixed width of bars </a>\r\n          </div>\r\n          <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n            <tbody>\r\n              <tr>\r\n                <td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\"> <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\"> Dennis Murphy\r\n                    <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;djm...@gmail.com&gt;</a>: Jan 27 01:21PM -0800 </span>\r\n                  <br>\r\n                  <br>\r\n                  Hi:<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  Here are a couple of suggestions. I think the first is\r\n                  what you were after.<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  library(ggplot2)<br>\r\n                  ggplot(dataset, aes(x = factor(station), y = var)) +<br>\r\n                  geom_bar(stat = &quot;identity&quot;, col = &quot;black&quot;, fill =\r\n                  &quot;white&quot;) +<br>\r\n                  facet_grid(. ~ area, scales = &quot;free_x&quot;, space =\r\n                  &quot;free&quot;) +<br>\r\n                  labs(x= &quot;station&quot;)<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  The &quot;free_x&quot; argument allows for varying numbers of\r\n                  levels per facet;<br>\r\n                  the space = &quot;free&quot; argument resizes the space\r\n                  proportionally in each<br>\r\n                  facet to the number of available levels.<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  As far as the labels are concerned, your request is\r\n                  possible but<br>\r\n                  requires some surgery with the grid and gtable\r\n                  packages. The<br>\r\n                  suggestion to facet by area is simpler and\r\n                  accomplishes the same<br>\r\n                  purpose.<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  An alternative to this is a Cleveland dot chart. I\r\n                  prefer the way it&#39;s<br>\r\n                  done in base graphics, where spacing is used to\r\n                  separate groups rather<br>\r\n                  than faceting. A basic version would be<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  with(dataset, dotchart(var, labels = station, groups =\r\n                  area, pch = 16))<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  Dennis<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                </td>\r\n              </tr>\r\n            </tbody>\r\n          </table>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\"> <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_2970457510136618189_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\">Back to top</a> </div>\r\n          <a name=\"m_2970457510136618189_group_thread_2\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a>\r\n          <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\"> <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/t/7bc337a1e969f920?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2/t/7bc337a1e969f920?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792369699250000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jGGAZcuoGQH21tOVPdJp3\"> Rcpp dependency not installed - was\r\n              &quot;RE: [R] installing Packages&quot; </a> </div>\r\n          <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n            <tbody>\r\n              <tr>\r\n                <td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\"> <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\"> Brian Diggs\r\n                    <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;brian....@gmail.com&gt;</a>: Jan 27 10:22AM\r\n                    -0800 </span> <br>\r\n                  <br>\r\n                  On 1/27/15 5:03 AM, S Ellison wrote:<br>\r\n                  &gt; there is a ggplot2 dependency on, or import from,\r\n                  Rcpp at all, and<br>\r\n                  &gt; the listed reverse depends/imports for Rcpp don’t\r\n                  include any of the<br>\r\n                  &gt; imports in ggplot2 either.<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  There is at least an indirect relationship. Both plyr\r\n                  and reshape2, <br>\r\n                  which are imports of ggplot2, import from Rcpp.<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  &gt; Could that be why the default (NA) for<br>\r\n                  &gt; dependencies is not picking up and installing\r\n                  Rcpp?<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  I don&#39;t believe so. I just tried installing ggplot2 in\r\n                  an empty library <br>\r\n                  (with only the recommended packages available in the\r\n                  system library) and <br>\r\n                  I got<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  &gt; install.packages(&quot;ggplot2&quot;)<br>\r\n                  Installing package into\r\n                  ‘/Users/schnade/Library/R/3.1/library’<br>\r\n                  (as ‘lib’ is unspecified)<br>\r\n                  also installing the dependencies ‘colorspace’, ‘Rcpp’,\r\n                  ‘stringr’, <br>\r\n                  ‘RColorBrewer’, ‘dichromat’, ‘munsell’, ‘labeling’,\r\n                  ‘plyr’, ‘digest’, <br>\r\n                  ‘gtable’, ‘reshape2’, ‘scales’, ‘proto’<br>\r\n                  [...rest of output not shown...]<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  &gt; &quot;Rcpp&quot; %in% rownames(installed.packages())<br>\r\n                  [1] TRUE<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  So Rcpp would get installed with the default\r\n                  arguments.<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  &gt; I&#39;ve cc&#39;d to the google group (I hope) to permit\r\n                  further discussion<br>\r\n                  &gt; there.<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  My guess as to what happened (and this is based on it\r\n                  having happened to <br>\r\n                  me before with a different package) is that something\r\n                  failed in the Rcpp <br>\r\n                  installation (as simple as a network timeout) and that\r\n                  fact got buried <br>\r\n                  in the output which went scrolling by. Failing to\r\n                  install one of the <br>\r\n                  dependencies does not actually make the installation\r\n                  of the package <br>\r\n                  fail. The next time it would show up as a problem\r\n                  would be when loading <br>\r\n                  the package.<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                  --Brian Diggs<br>\r\n                   <br>\r\n                </td>\r\n              </tr>\r\n            </tbody>\r\n          </table>\r\n          <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\"> <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_2970457510136618189_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\">Back to top</a> </div>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <div style=\"background-color:#f5f5f5;padding:5px 20px\">\r\n          <table style=\"width:100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n            <tbody>\r\n              <tr>\r\n                <td style=\"padding-top:4px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:#636363;font-size:11px\">\r\n                  You received this digest because you&#39;re subscribed to\r\n                  updates for this group. You can change your settings\r\n                  on the <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" rel=\"nofollow\">group\r\n                    membership page</a>.<br>\r\n                  To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving\r\n                  emails from it send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r\n                </td>\r\n              </tr>\r\n            </tbody>\r\n          </table>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </blockquote>\r\n    <br>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  }
